Font attribution
----------------

The renderer ships with **no font files**. At runtime it auto-detects one of
the following families, in this order (see ``lyric_mv/config.py``):

* Source Han Serif SC Heavy — SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Adobe / Google / Changzhou SinoType. Source of the dramatic serif look used
  by the bundled ``F_aurora_ribbon`` style.

* Noto Serif SC, Noto Sans SC — SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Google. Cross-platform open-source fallback.

* Source Han Sans CN, Source Han Serif SC — SIL Open Font License 1.1

If you do not have any of these installed, run ``python scripts/fetch_fonts.py``
which downloads the Noto family into ``assets/fonts/`` (≈ 40 MB total).

System fonts such as Dengb (DengXian Bold), msyh.ttc (Microsoft YaHei) and
PingFang.ttc are NOT redistributable. They are used only as last-resort
fallbacks when the OFL families above are unavailable, and never bundled.


Reference song assets
---------------------

The bundled showcase images in ``showcase/`` are redrawn from the same design
tokens as the renderer; no audio or full-frame video from any reference song is
included in this repository. Full song audio and masters live in a separate
non-public archive.